/// Terminal (dev) backend for the `text` device — merged under `ARCHE_SELECT=text=terminal`. For the native
/// `arche run` dev loop (`make dev`): there is no browser DOM to render into, so instead of drawing glyphs
/// this echoes each `text.draw` to stdout via the text_term.c shim (auto-discovered from this variant folder;
/// pure libc, so no `#link`). It lets a text-using program (e.g. src/scene.arche) run NATIVELY — hot-reload,
/// x11 window for gfx — without the wasm/DOM host, printing the HUD strings to the console. Same `#foreign`
/// contract shape as text/wasm; the `text_be_*` symbols are `#module`-private. Not a standalone test.
// RUN: true
#module
#foreign
text_be_draw  :: proc(x: int, y: int, own s: []char, n: int, size: int, color: int);
text_be_clear :: proc();
